  {
   "id": 1,
   "ref": "99–104",
   "en": "'Why do we not instead make a lasting peace and an agreed marriage? You have exactly what you set your whole heart on: Dido is burning with love and has drawn the madness right through her bones. Let us, then, rule this people in common, with equal authority between us; let her be allowed to serve a Trojan husband, and hand her Tyrians over to you as her dowry.'",
   "en_marked": "'[Why do we not|1] [instead|2] [make|7] a [lasting|4] [peace|3] [and|5] [an agreed|5] [marriage|6]? [You have|8] {exactly|Not in the Latin. Added for emphasis.} [what|10] [you set|12] your [whole|9] [heart|11] [on|12]: [Dido|15] [is burning|13] [with love|14] [and|16] [has drawn|16] the [madness|19] [right through|17] her [bones|18]. [Let us|25], [then|22], [rule|25] [this|21] [people|23] [in common|20], with [equal|24] [authority|26] {between us|Not in the Latin. Added to make clear that the equal auspices are shared by Juno and Venus.}; [let her be allowed|27] [to serve|29] a [Trojan|28] [husband|30], [and|31] [hand|34] her [Tyrians|33] [over|34] [to you|32,35] as her [dowry|31].'",
