  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "105–109",
   "en": "Venus knew well enough that Juno had spoken with false intent, meaning to turn the kingdom of Italy aside to the shores of Libya instead, and [answered|15,16] her in turn: 'Who would be mad enough to refuse an offer like that, or choose to [go to war|25,26] with you — if only fortune [follows through on|33,31] what you propose?",
   "en_marked": "[Venus|17] [knew|2] {well enough|Not in the Latin as such. Added for emphasis; the Latin has only sensit enim (for she sensed).} that {Juno|Added for clarity: the Latin only has the participle locutam, so the translator names Juno.} [had spoken|6] with [false|4] [intent|5], [meaning to|7] [turn|11] the [kingdom|8] [of Italy|9] [aside|11] to the [shores|12] [of Libya|10] {instead|Not in the Latin. Added to bring out the idea of diverting the kingdom in averteret.}, and [answered|15,16] [her|1] [in turn|14]: '[Who|18] would be [mad|20] enough to [refuse|21] an {offer|Added for clarity: talia just means such things, so the translator names what Juno is offering.} [like that|19], [or|22] [choose|24] to [go to war|25,26] [with you|23] — [if|27] [only|28] [fortune|32] [follows through on|33,31] [what|29] [you propose|30]?",
